{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal","id":844585,"title":"How Fighty are Sidereal ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-09T10:19:10-08:00","id":844585,"title":"How Fighty are Sidereal ?","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgbox.com/tsLQU4aJ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> Sadly I have no idea what Sidereal mechanic looks like in Ex1, but from what I heard they can pretty much make everyone smell their fart in combat, but this stems from the fact they abuse the system I think (something about persistence/rolled defense), Ex2 Sid is not much better. SMAs are also broken in both Edition so their purpose in the setting and powerlevel is still a mystery to me, are they high Essence Sid charm disguise as MA, or are they &quot;stuff for NPC only&quot; since no starting Sid will ever have SMA at chargen due to the way gaining Essence now work,.<br /> <br /> Now that Ex3 is rolling, can I ask what exactly are Sidereal/SMA power level ? Like, what kind of tactic that they usually employ to get the most out of their charm, what will make them scream like a baby. What are some mechanic/charm effect that are exclusive to them, which are the one that they don't have. Are they still Offense &gt; Defense: The Splat, since I'm not really sure how to survive at chargen when I can only increase my Defense by freaking one ! Not every Sid has a Solar bodyguard with Defend Other suite you know....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:30:13-08:00","id":844596,"title":"","content":"Every time I ask about Sidereals in Ex3, I get the &quot;It's too soon to know&quot; answer. I'm really hoping that they will have more charms that in Ex2. Combat-wise, I hope they are able to do all sorts of Funky things with Initiative, like steal from enemies or switch initiative scores with allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:34:19-08:00","id":844599,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, Solar has like....600 charms I think ? I seriously want more charms per tree for Sidereal ! I cry every time I look at Sidereal Investigation :'(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:43:22-08:00","id":844606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844599#post844599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, Solar has like....600 charms I think ? I seriously want more charms per tree for Sidereal ! I cry every time I look at Sidereal Investigation :'(</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's like the writers for Ex2 forgot the Capstone Investigation Charm. All the other Charm Trees have a Essence 4 Charm.<br /> <br /> I also want more charms that interact with the Loom of Fate. Or more guidance on how to interact with the Loom of Fate. I think in the Ex2 book, it simply an Investigation Roll. Of course, I don't want to have to do Destiny Taxes (what my Friday Night Skype Group calls Astrology) to be able to find information on the Loom, but I do want some sort guidelines that aren't just Storyteller Fiat.<br /> <br /> (I have some homebrew notes on how to interact with the Loom that I really need to type up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:50:11-08:00","id":844609,"title":"","content":"Based on the QuickStart rules alone they are amazing because TN reduction is amazing. Who cares if your dice adding is limited if you need to roll a 4 or better on any given die?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:57:09-08:00","id":844614,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the sample Sid can lower the TN on damage rolls.<br /> <br /> On DAMAGE ROLLS, GUYS.<br /> <br /> Five Seasons Approach lowers the TN by one on a decisive attack automatically. If fired on a Crashed enemy, it's lowered by another point, and if your Initiative is 12 or more it's lowered by ANOTHER point.<br /> <br /> So if a Sidereal with 14 Initiative uses Five Seasons Approach on a crashed enemy, the Decisive Damage TN is <b>4</b>.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Sids look like if they want to be, they can be <i>lethal</i>. Though... Your Defenses will be a bit weaker on an Excellency front. You can only add +[Essence] points to your static values with your Excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:00:43-08:00","id":844618,"title":"","content":"I would not extrapolate anything like that from the QC Sidereal rules. Thematic stuff sure, but balance-wise I'd assume they will tweak anything that's overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:01:38-08:00","id":844619,"title":"","content":"Adding to static values isn't even the great power of charms, though it is nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:06:20-08:00","id":844622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844619#post844619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding to static values isn't even the great power of charms, though it is nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still have shitty dice cap for their Defense though, I expect a Sidereal to die quickly unless they have some means to mess with the opponent attack dicepool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:09:30-08:00","id":844626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844622#post844622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They still have shitty dice cap for their Defense though, I expect a Sidereal to die quickly unless they have some means to mess with the opponent attack dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>y'know, it could be a pretty neat charm/feature for siddies if they had a defense bonus against things inside of fate... Just a thought..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:13:58-08:00","id":844630,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd settle with after about 100-150 exp I don't feel completely lost on wtf to get next. Does anyone actually enforce the no custom Sid charms rule and do we know if that god forsaken rule is staying? I'm getting tired of constantly having to homebrew for a splat that already has a million little bonus rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:16:05-08:00","id":844631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844622#post844622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They still have shitty dice cap for their Defense though, I expect a Sidereal to die quickly unless they have some means to mess with the opponent attack dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Dodge Tree is full of fun tricks. Admittedly, we haven't seen many of their Defense Charms.<br /> <br /> The sample one has a soak-boosting charm that also creates a pool of Initiative that gets drained first by withering attacks, for example.<br /> <br /> And one that reduces the damage pool of a decisive attack against them, as well as raising the TN of the opponent's damage roll by one.<br /> <br /> So yeah, fucking with an opponent's dice seems to be entirely in-theme. Raising the TN of a damage roll from 7 to 8... Well I'm not very good at statistics but I imagine that it sufficiently Makes Things Tougher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:34:24-08:00","id":844633,"title":"","content":"They're pretty hardcore.<br /> <br /> They're celestial Exalted and peerless masters of the martial arts, so...even if they literally had no native Charms except Excellencies, they'd be pretty tough in a fight. And you can expect their native combat Charms to be competitive with their Martial Arts Charms, because they wouldn't be worth taking otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:32:50-08:00","id":844672,"title":"","content":"Oh, and don't forget, when a Sid uses Marital Arts? They may well have the Mystical Advantage that lets them access the Mastery keyword of their MA Charms. So there's <i>that</i>.<br /> <br /> For comparison, I recently had a Night Martial Artist in my group oneshot a buck-ogre, using ONLY Snake and Ebon Shadow Charms.<br /> <br /> WITHOUT making any withering attacks. Just *Appear, strike, shadow noose, dead*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:34:55-08:00","id":844674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844622#post844622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They still have shitty dice cap for their Defense though, I expect a Sidereal to die quickly unless they have some means to mess with the opponent attack dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not accurate considering how the combat system<br /> Is two tiered this edition. Any round you attack is a round where it's hard to kill you absent some odds that Sidereals will very likely have ways to avoid anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844633#post844633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you can expect their native combat Charms to be competitive with their Martial Arts Charms, because they wouldn't be worth taking otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect this but then again I don't expect the 3e Sid native charm set to be unplayable garbage for the better part of 10 years like 2e's was, so. <br /> <br /> Not stacking with MA doesn't inherently make Sid combat Charms worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-09-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:36:04-08:00","id":844676,"title":"","content":"So, first off I think that Zel is right - the Fateful Excellency is <i>flippin' </i>awesome. If all you ever got was base dice pools plus that thing, you'd already be a powerhouse.<br /> <br /> But Sids <i>do </i>get lots more than that, don't they? Like incredibly good access to sorcery, one of the most flexible and powerful systems 3E has to offer. And access to heavenly Artifacts and all the Evocations they provide. And Martial Arts, which we have been told is incredibly scary and which the Sidereals are the <i>undisputed masters </i>of. So...like, how fighty are Sidereals? They can be fighty as shit without hardly even touching <i>their own native Charm-set</i>, which we should probably assume will be competitive with all those other systems since the design team wants the players to have actual choices.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are gonna be scary as all hell, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:41:40-08:00","id":844681,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't take the QCs as representing anything line what those splats are actually capable of. Those QCs are supposed to be credible antagonists with only 4 charms.<br /> <br /> For sure the sids, lunars and DBs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T13:21:22-08:00","id":844691,"title":"","content":"Intuitively, I'd hope there'd be lots of potential to imagine how Sidereal Charms can interact with the Initiative / Withering combat momentum system. Sidereals can fight in such a manner that the universe recognises the auspicious essence of their techniques and reaches out to turn the tables in their favour - such is written and such shall it be! When you fight against them, things seem to smoothly go in their advantage even they worryingly don't seem to be actually *doing* that much! (Not doing much, to the unrefined eyes of one lacking in attunement to and perception of the proper symbols, signs and motifs of fate, at least).<br /> <br /> Having that abstracted measure of advantage prominent seems like it offers good hooks for the Sidereal schtick that were harder when everything was measured more in more concrete resources and dice probabilities by default (and so things are being modeled more often by blatantly sorcerous and supernatural magic or by effects like &quot;You get more Essence / Dice, under this condition&quot;, etc). That said, I'm not actually sure if there's much mechanically that much fresh ground there to be had, so! grain of salt on all the above. (Particularly not after discounting stuff that = mechanical knightmare).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T13:31:20-08:00","id":844695,"title":"","content":"How useful were the greater astrology charms for combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T14:09:55-08:00","id":844726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844695#post844695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How useful were the greater astrology charms for combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one I can vouch for is Inevitability Without Finesse.<br /> It's one of the only things I'd say is approrpiately balanced by a mechanic as punative as the Pattern Bite in that you could completely stonewall the First and Forsaken Lion for multiple actions until your Paradox track fills up and if that doesn't take you out the fight you could hypothetically hold him up for another 10 actions and take the gamble again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:30:43-08:00","id":845272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844630#post844630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd settle with after about 100-150 exp I don't feel completely lost on wtf to get next. Does anyone actually enforce the no custom Sid charms rule and do we know if that god forsaken rule is staying? I'm getting tired of constantly having to homebrew for a splat that already has a million little bonus rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty sure one of the Devs said that they will be capping the Sidereal Charmset this edition but that was a while ago. So we're back to too soon to know. I also can't remember where it was said...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:36:20-08:00","id":845274,"title":"","content":"A chosen of Battles should be pretty Battley","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/957-wulfram","name":"Wulfram","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:39:08-08:00","id":845279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844674#post844674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect this but then again I don't expect the 3e Sid native charm set to be unplayable garbage for the better part of 10 years like 2e's was, so.<br /> <br /> Not stacking with MA doesn't inherently make Sid combat Charms worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might've misread my post.<br /> <br /> I didn't say they'd stack with MA (though that seems like a good idea to me), I just said they'd be competitive with MA. So the choice between a Martial Arts Charm and a native Sidereal Charm isn't trivial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:03:58-08:00","id":845290,"title":"","content":"I imagine that Sidereals will be at least decent at fighting most things, without being calibrated for full-on Exalt vs Exalt fights in which everybody is built like a player character, because that isn't really the default play direction of the game. In cases where it <i>does</i> happen... yes, I would say that a Sidereal good at things other than Martial Arts is at a bit of a disadvantage if the goal is to kill the other person. If it's to effectively get away alive or do something that will persistently mess their enemy up, I'd say they have some pretty significant advantages. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want more charms that interact with the Loom of Fate. Or more guidance on how to interact with the Loom of Fate. I think in the Ex2 book, it simply an Investigation Roll. Of course, I don't want to have to do Destiny Taxes (what my Friday Night Skype Group calls Astrology) to be able to find information on the Loom, but I do want some sort guidelines that aren't just Storyteller Fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm kind of hoping that the Loom of Fate won't really operate as this big independent thing that goes by rules unrelated to Sidereal Charms this time around. It's like, when you strike somebody's name from the book of love, or seek out the hidden vessels in which a set of gods hid the worst secrets of the world, or grow a tree that is adorned with clues for solving your problem, or assault somebody with visions of their own eventual death, you're &quot;interacting with the Loom of Fate&quot;. Comments by Holden suggesting that something like the concept of being &quot;outside of Fate&quot; might not even be in the game at all anymore give me hope for a somewhat less mechanistic Loom; that's not even a question of the value of mysteries, just that the way they tried to describe the thing before made it a bit of a pain to figure out what it actually was and how it worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:15:52-08:00","id":845303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845290#post845290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that Sidereals will be at least decent at fighting most things, without being calibrated for full-on Exalt vs Exalt fights in which everybody is built like a player character, because that isn't really the default play direction of the game. In cases where it <i>does</i> happen... yes, I would say that a Sidereal good at things other than Martial Arts is at a bit of a disadvantage if the goal is to kill the other person. If it's to effectively get away alive or do something that will persistently mess their enemy up, I'd say they have some pretty significant advantages. I'm kind of hoping that the Loom of Fate won't really operate as this big independent thing that goes by rules unrelated to Sidereal Charms this time around. It's like, when you strike somebody's name from the book of love, or seek out the hidden vessels in which a set of gods hid the worst secrets of the world, or grow a tree that is adorned with clues for solving your problem, or assault somebody with visions of their own eventual death, you're &quot;interacting with the Loom of Fate&quot;. Comments by Holden suggesting that something like the concept of being &quot;outside of Fate&quot; might not even be in the game at all anymore give me hope for a somewhat less mechanistic Loom; that's not even a question of the value of mysteries, just that the way they tried to describe the thing before made it a bit of a pain to figure out what it actually was and how it worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have considered the idea that the Loom of Fate isn't some building in Yu-Shan but some meta-physical force Sidereals interact with in Creation via Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:21:41-08:00","id":845311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844681#post844681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't take the QCs as representing anything line what those splats are actually capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure the QCs are going to change some of the details but I'll be shocked if the way, say, Excellencies work for Sidereal PCs is different than for QuickStart NPCs, because then you run into the issue of the 2e ST guide giving antagonists which were pretty quickly obsoleted by their own splatbook rules, and nobody liked that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:25:39-08:00","id":845314,"title":"","content":"No, I would definitely still want it to be a gigantic series of poles and complexly woven threads managed by a society of robot spider gods. Just not so much the idea of &quot;Sidereals have their own Charms for one kind of foresight, and this entirely different kind of foresight they get from manually looking at the actual threads, which is a lot more complicated and has a lot more rules and limits&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T16:33:24-08:00","id":845343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845314#post845314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I would definitely still want it to be a gigantic series of poles and complexly woven threads managed by a society of robot spider gods. Just not so much the idea of &quot;Sidereals have their own Charms for one kind of foresight, and this entirely different kind of foresight they get from manually looking at the actual threads, which is a lot more complicated and has a lot more rules and limits&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also want gods of a certain rank and other exalts to be able to interact with the Loom of Fate. I'm thinking like its the arbitrator of what happens to Mortals and Spirits, but also is used as punishment for those Outside Fate. Those Oustside of Fate can't be targeted by the subtle powers of the Loom, but can be declared &quot;Unholy&quot; and that is why Cold Iron, salt, grains, and Thaurmaturgic wards/ Holy attacks work on them. Its also the reason why Eclipses have there powers and why oaths are very binding to Fae in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T16:53:15-08:00","id":845350,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with Gods in Bureau of Destiny having access to the Loom, but not other Exalts. Except maybe those new anti - Sidereal Exalts that I can't remember how to spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:04:49-08:00","id":845356,"title":"","content":"It's pretty hard to judge what fighty Sidereals are going to look like in 3e because the example fighty Sidereal uses Violet Bier charms, which are rad but may not be representative of what the native trees look like. That said, they apparently have some way to access Mastery effects on regular MAs, which are insanely great, and given that Holden likes fighty stuff and likes Sidereals I can't imagine he'll let them go without love. I expect they'll still be somewhat &quot;high-execution&quot; in a straight fight, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:25:42-08:00","id":845365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want gods of a certain rank and other exalts to be able to interact with the Loom of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div> This gets at a problem I have seperate from the whole thing of &quot;Sidereals have a form of divination other than their actual Charms&quot; which amounts to &quot;absolutely everybody has the things that they can do, plus the Loom of Fate&quot;. Oh, you want to make it rain frogs on an enemy? Well, you can be the type with that as your own Charms, you can use Sorcery, or the Loom of Fate. I find it sets the whole thing up in this nebulous space in which it's a kind of I Win button for the universe, or else it's kind of perfunctory. I suppose what I'm saying is that I feel that the Loom should exist, just be supposed to be working independently 90% of the time, and be the basic background of magic to interact with Fate such as Sidereals or certain gods. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> is used as punishment for those Outside Fate</div> </div> </div> </div> Assuming that that's even really a concept. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurseteller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">can be declared &quot;Unholy&quot; and that is why Cold Iron, salt, grains, and Thaurmaturgic wards/ Holy attacks work on them. Its also the reason why Eclipses have there powers and why oaths are very binding to Fae in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div> That seems a bit overwrought to me. Also, oaths are binding to raksha everywhere, and to everyone. Actually, looking more closely at it... that's <i>another</i> issue I have with the Loom; it establishes a premise in which certain things might look as though they should retroactively be associated with it, which to me feels like either a dumbass late-game reveal or an appropriation. It's a bit like how after those Infernal Heresy Charms came out, a lot of people wanted to transmit the concept to everything. The Eclipse Anima power really shouldn't have anything to do with the Loom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:15:32-08:00","id":845410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845365#post845365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Eclipse Anima power really shouldn't have anything to do with the Loom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, in prior editions the diplomatic immunity part of the Eclipse Anima power isn't even technically a <i>power</i>, is it? It's just &quot;the Eclipse Caste is <i>so good</i> at negotiating that they managed to negotiate diplomatic immunity for themselves as a class of being even with the raksha in the Deep Wyld and the Neverborn.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T23:30:13-08:00","id":845494,"title":"","content":"For now, as it's a long time to 3e Sidereals, I tend to find the best thing to do is assume Sidereals are masters of martial arts, and use the martial arts (especially the more esoteric ones) as their combat charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T23:36:42-08:00","id":845495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845272#post845272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure one of the Devs said that they will be capping the Sidereal Charmset this edition but that was a while ago. So we're back to too soon to know. I also can't remember where it was said...</div> </div> </div> </div>This will not, however, stop them adding new Charms to the Charmset if necessary - they'll just be treated as always having been there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T23:56:17-08:00","id":845502,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm sure they'll have both a different, and much bigger charmset, even if the idea that they can't make custom charms is still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T00:40:03-08:00","id":845507,"title":"","content":"What's going to be interesting about the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded is that, really, this is sort of the first time since... ever... they're getting a proper Charmset overhaul. A lot of 2e for those two groups was &quot;tweak the 1e Charms to work with the revised combat engine.&quot; This ain't that. We're likely getting a full-on rebuild, like the Solars got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T01:08:10-08:00","id":845518,"title":"","content":"I certainly hope so, and not just because that charmset wasn't well written.<br /> I found the extra stuff made in 2.5 (like Throne Shadow style) seemed to fit Sidereal themes a lot better than the actual charmset in their book did. Sidereal Firearms and Drive too, but of course they don't fit well into many games! But it showed that the writers of late 2.5, most of whom are the writers of 3e, seemed to have a much better idea of how to do a Sidereal charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T02:05:59-08:00","id":845529,"title":"","content":"Better idea than whom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:35:48-08:00","id":845746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845356#post845356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty hard to judge what fighty Sidereals are going to look like in 3e because the example fighty Sidereal uses Violet Bier charms, which are rad but may not be representative of what the native trees look like. That said, they apparently have some way to access Mastery effects on regular MAs, which are insanely great, and given that Holden likes fighty stuff and likes Sidereals I can't imagine he'll let them go without love. I expect they'll still be somewhat &quot;high-execution&quot; in a straight fight, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're an archer, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:42:41-08:00","id":845748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845746#post845746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're an archer, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though in the Layout Leak, the example Bronze Faction <i>was</i> a Martial Artist who used Violet Bier charms. The leak also had a Gold Faction Sidereal who may be used to aid the Solar PCs. But for wordcount they apparently axed the Gold Faction member, and changed the Swordsman into an Archer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:38:00-08:00","id":845810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845356#post845356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty hard to judge what fighty Sidereals are going to look like in 3e because the example fighty Sidereal uses Violet Bier charms, which are rad but may not be representative of what the native trees look like. That said, they apparently have some way to access Mastery effects on regular MAs, which are insanely great, and given that Holden likes fighty stuff and likes Sidereals I can't imagine he'll let them go without love. I expect they'll still be somewhat &quot;high-execution&quot; in a straight fight, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>High execution makes fine, I guess, if it's a natural outcome of just exploring mechanics that aren't the most intuitive and straightforward ones that crop up early in the line. I would look a bit askance at any of the writers making them high execution-ish because Sidereals are *supposed* to be only for expert players or something. I look at it more as when Sidereals as a whole already got an odd concept, it makes more sense to try, if anything, to make them more straightforward to understand mechanically, to make them more approachable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845518#post845518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found the extra stuff made in 2.5 (like Throne Shadow style) seemed to fit Sidereal themes a lot better than the actual charmset in their book did. Sidereal Firearms and Drive too, but of course they don't fit well into many games! But it showed that the writers of late 2.5, most of whom are the writers of 3e, seemed to have a much better idea of how to do a Sidereal charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any in particular? I kind of only know, by reputation here, about the gunfingers one, which was kind of... for me.... Charm brings the cutesy, but where is the mythic?<br /> <br /> Throne Shadow is... kind of hard for me to love, because it feels pretty literal about Sidereals being powers being the throne for me. It's like if you were excited about buying Performance, then Sidereal Performance gave you cascades of Charms themed on being a secret choirmaster rather than actual performances like the Song of Spirit Persuasion, which your Sidereal does. Although that's not probably the greatest example, it sort of gets at the spirit. Seems like Throne Shadow sort of seems to undermine the choice the player made to intentionally buy an active, personal ability as opposed to an organizing ability, in the first place. &quot;So you took an ability that's about doing rather than controlling others to do? Tough. This is what you get.&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:25:52-08:00","id":845866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845507#post845507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A lot of 2e for those two groups was &quot;tweak the 1e Charms to work with the revised combat engine.&quot; This ain't that. We're likely getting a full-on rebuild, like the Solars got.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really generous that you even call it &quot;tweaking.&quot; I think it's more like &quot;bad copypasta done by people who didn't know how the new mechanics worked and didn't care to learn.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T11:56:16-08:00","id":846198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=845748#post845748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though in the Layout Leak, the example Bronze Faction <i>was</i> a Martial Artist who used Violet Bier charms. The leak also had a Gold Faction Sidereal who may be used to aid the Solar PCs. But for wordcount they apparently axed the Gold Faction member, and changed the Swordsman into an Archer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's the mistake. Doh! I haven't been through the Antagonists in sufficient detail since the backer pdf. OK, let me look at this one.<br /> <br /> Ah, that's actually very cool and stompy! I agree it's probably buffed a bit relative to what we'll see in their hardback but it makes me excited to see how other splats interface with 3e's mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T12:04:51-08:00","id":846206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=844614#post844614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the sample Sid can lower the TN on damage rolls.<br /> <br /> On DAMAGE ROLLS, GUYS.<br /> <br /> Five Seasons Approach lowers the TN by one on a decisive attack automatically. If fired on a Crashed enemy, it's lowered by another point, and if your Initiative is 12 or more it's lowered by ANOTHER point.<br /> <br /> So if a Sidereal with 14 Initiative uses Five Seasons Approach on a crashed enemy, the Decisive Damage TN is <b>4</b>.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Sids look like if they want to be, they can be <i>lethal</i>. Though... Your Defenses will be a bit weaker on an Excellency front. You can only add +[Essence] points to your static values with your Excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what a TN is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T12:18:55-08:00","id":846211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=846206#post846206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what a TN is...</div> </div> </div> </div>Target number, what WoD called difficulty. The number on each die that you have to match or beat for it to count as a success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T12:25:24-08:00","id":846216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/844585-how-fighty-are-sidereal?p=846206#post846206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what a TN is...</div> </div> </div> </div>Target number! Like instead of needing at least a 7 for a success, you need at least a 6, or 5, or 4 or whatever. At higher initiative it's hands down the best decisive damage adder in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"